From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:06:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] middleware: the Plugins row says how many calls a middleware
 changed (#4271)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A middleware that acts on some requests only read as if it had acted on
all of them: the row counted every call of its hooks alike (m.calls in
Run.apply), so unisong's middleware-codex-history passing a third
provider's requests through unchanged read "onRequest · 2 calls" like
two rewritten ones. A plugin can't count for itself: onRequest runs on
every request, the provider is only known inside the call, and a pure
middleware has nowhere the Plugins page shows.

State gains Changed: the calls whose hook changed something. A returned
body is one (onRequest, onProvider, onEvent, onResponse), as are a
dropped event (onEvent returning null), a turned-away request (ctx.
reject in onRequest) and a passed-over account ({skip: true} in
onAccount). A call whose hook passed its input through unchanged
(undefined) and one that failed are calls, not changes. The count
sits where the call's outcome is already told (Request, Tried,
Account, writer.event, writer.finish), so the hot path adds one atomic
add on a change and nothing on a pass-through. The row says changed
when it differs from calls, in every language i18n.js has;
gateway-middleware.md says what Changed counts.

Fixes #4271

Tests:
- TestChangedCounts: one middleware with all five hooks. A pass-through
  request (undefined) is a call, not a change; a returned body, a
  reject, a {skip: true} account, a dropped event (onEvent null) and a
  whole-reply rewrite are changes, one each; a thrown call is a failure,
  not a change. TestOnProvider now says Changed too: three of its five
  tries returned a body, the throw and the null didn't.
- plugin-middleware.test.cjs: the fake row's middleware counts 12,345
  calls and 12,340 changed, and the row says so in English and Chinese.

Run (mote, darwin/arm64):
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/middleware/: ok. gofmt -l:
  clean. go vet -tags nogui ./internal/middleware/: clean. go build
  -tags nogui .: ok.
- node --test internal/gui/tests/plugin-middleware.test.cjs on
  chromium: 12 of 12 ok.

Broken by hand, each with a real FAIL and then restored:
- the seven m.changed.Add(1) lines taken out of run.go and account.go:
  TestChangedCounts red ("after a change: ... Changed:0") and
  TestOnProvider red ("changed ... Changed:0"). Restored: ok.
- plugins.js's mwLine taken back to the one-line stats: the
  plugin-middleware test red in en and zh (the row read "12,345 calls,
  0.9 µs each", the test wants "12,345 calls, 12,340 changed, 0.9 µs
  each"). Restored: 12 of 12 ok.

